+    'reconstruction': "A drawing reconstruction method for the supplied originals.\n\nEstablish the building's perimeter, physical dividers and openings from the\nwhole drawing and suitable clean enlargements. Follow each divider through its\njunctions and door symbols, and each space around its complete boundary.\nRepresent a drawn internal wall by its centre line when that matches the\ndimensioned layout; identify the reference plane of exterior dimensions too.\nWall fill colour is a drawing convention. Use the complete linework, junctions,\ndoor symbols and relevant dimensions together to decide whether a divider exists.\n\nUse readable dimension labels with their actual extension endpoints to derive\nthe layout in a consistent frame. Check units and a second known span on each\naxis. Use map_pixels/map_dimension_chain for arithmetic. Where labels do not\nresolve a position, measure the relevant local feature with the available pixel\ntools and state the chosen representative plane. A profile answers the selected\nlocal pixel question; assess that question's relevance to the physical object.\nAll submitted pixel coordinates refer to the original image. Apply the crop's\nreported transform when interpreting a cropped or resized view. Selected saved\nmeasurements can be referenced directly in plan declarations when useful.\n\nKeep stable door/window identities across plan and elevation. Use facade,\nstorey, order, complete span and adjacent features to match each opening, then\nread its actual sill/head or applicable dimension chain. Check each distinct\nheight family before sharing values. Preserve exceptions, including small or\ntall windows. State assumptions for properties absent from the supplied views.\n\nBuild the physical paths and apertures with the existing deterministic tools.\nInspect the saved source plan, original overlay and relevant source elevations.\nCompare actual dividers, spaces on both sides, complete opening spans and height\nfamilies to the originals. On a conflict, reobserve the affected original object,\nrevise the supported property locally, and inspect the saved change and affected\nhosts/connections. Keep unrelated declarations intact. A self-consistent model\nor confirmation of a saved value does not establish its correspondence to the\ndrawing. Finish with the actual remaining uncertainties and completed scope.\n",
